UPDATE companies SET description='Aletheia Design & Sewing Service operates from a compact facility in the Northeast Minneapolis arts district NE. Founded in 2014, the company is owned and operated by Abby Hansen, a garment technician with over 12 years of industrial apparel experience. Hansen’s background includes soft‑goods production management, contract sewing, and costume work for Sesame Street Live, the Minnesota Opera, and the Guthrie Theater. She holds a BA in Apparel Design from St. Catherine University, a certificate in Apparel Technologies from Minneapolis Community and Technical College, and is an alumna of the Sewing Factory School’s Apparel Manufacturing Boot Camp. The name “aletheia” (Greek for “disclosure” or “unconcealedness”) reflects a commitment to transparency in fashion manufacturing.

The shop provides a la carte product‑development and cut‑and‑sew services for emerging brands. Core processes include pattern making, fit audits, sample making, grading coordination, marker making, and small‑batch production runs of 20 to 200 units per style per colorway. Equipment comprises Union Special, Rimoldi, Juki, and Singer industrial sewing machines plus dedicated cutting space. The low‑overhead, human‑scale workspace is designed to keep costs manageable for small‑order clients.

Aletheia serves young, local, and small apparel brands that need technical guidance and flexible manufacturing to launch their lines. Customers range from independent designers with a single sketch to brands ready for presales and initial production runs. The collaborative development model lets clients engage only the steps they need, from initial consulting through to finished goods.

Hansen started the business to offer an affordable, low‑minimum alternative to traditional factories, emphasizing honesty in pricing and process. By keeping scope focused and referring out work outside her core capabilities, she aims to deliver quality garments within a startup’s budget.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Launch Audit Consult", "General Consulting", "Hard copy pattern making / Pattern Audit", "Fit Audit", "Samplemaking / Style Development", "Sourcing Kickstart Document", "Preproduction: Cutter''s must, Coordinate grading and marking", "Size sets / Duplicate samples", "Cut and bundle / Hard copy marker making", "Small batch cut and sew (20-200 units)", "Access to in-house guts, notions, and trim", "Grading coordination (referred)", "Production pattern making", "Contract sewing", "Cut and sew manufacturing", "Product development consulting", "Technical design consulting", "Sample making", "Marker making", "Fit auditing", "Sourcing assistance"], "industries": ["Apparel manufacturing", "Fashion design", "Soft goods manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Union Special industrial sewing machines", "Rimoldi industrial sewing machines", "Juki industrial sewing machines", "Singer industrial sewing machines", "Cutting tables"], "volume": "20 to 200 units per style per colorway", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low-minimum production runs (20 units per style per colorway)", "A la carte, collaborative product development model", "Low-overhead, human-scale factory in NE Minneapolis arts district", "Owner-operated with 12+ years industrial apparel and costume experience", "Referral network for services beyond in-house capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Located in Northeast Minneapolis arts district at 3134 California St NE -> /about", "Owned and operated by Abby Hansen -> /about", "Abby Hansen has 12+ years industrial apparel experience -> /about", "Background includes costume work for Sesame Street Live, MN Opera, Guthrie -> /about", "Education: BA Apparel Design St. Catherine University, certificate Apparel Technologies MCTC, Sewing Factory School Boot Camp alumna -> /about", "Offers low-minimum cut and sew (20-200 units per style per colorway) -> /services", "Equipment: Union Special, Rimoldi, Juki, Singer machines and cutting space -> /services", "Services: pattern making, fit audit, sample making, grading coordination, marker making, small batch production, consulting -> /services", "Serves emerging, local, small apparel brands -> /, /services", "Collaborative a la carte product development model -> /services", "Low-overhead, human-scale factory concept -> /about", "Name ''aletheia'' means disclosure/unconcealedness in Greek -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Apparel Cut and Sew in Minneapolis, Minnesota", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "20 units per style per colorway", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='aletheia-design-sewing-service' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alkar-RapidPak, Inc. is based in Lodi, Wisconsin, and traces its roots to the 1950s. The company operates as a division of Middleby Food Processing and Packaging, a global portfolio of food production brands. No founders are named in available sources.

The company custom engineers batch and continuous cooking and chilling equipment for the protein and alternative protein industries. Its product line includes batch ovens (500–50,000 lbs capacity), continuous processing systems (up to 10,000 lbs/hr), and high-performance chillers. Processes cover cooking, smoking, chilling, and pasteurization, with the proprietary TurboChef oven combining microwave, convection, and steam heating. To date, Alkar has installed nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units worldwide.

Customers span meat, poultry, alternative protein, pet food, fish, and snack processors globally. The company provides scientific advice, process development, plant layout, and custom equipment design alongside its hardware.

Alkar differentiates itself with the only industrial oven offering microwave, convection, and steam heating in a single unit, and emphasizes unwavering customer support and custom thermal processing solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineering", "Batch cooking", "Continuous cooking", "Chilling", "Smoking", "Pasteurization", "Process development", "Plant layout", "Custom equipment design", "Automation solutions", "Microwave heating", "Convection heating", "Steam heating", "TurboChef technology"], "industries": ["Meat", "Poultry", "Alternative Protein", "Pet Food", "Fish", "Snacks"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TurboChef", "Batch ovens", "Continuous processing systems", "Chillers"], "volume": "Batch systems 500\u201350,000 lbs capacity; continuous processing up to 10,000 lbs/hr", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only industrial oven with microwave, convection, and steam heating combined (TurboChef)", "Nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units installed worldwide", "Custom engineered batch and continuous cooking/chilling equipment", "Process development, plant layout, and custom equipment design services", "Automated continuous processing up to 10,000 lbs/hr"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lodi, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded in the 1950s -> /", "Division of Middleby Food Processing and Packaging -> /about-us", "Custom engineers batch and continuous cooking and chilling equipment -> /", "Batch ovens 500\u201350,000 lbs capacity -> /about-us", "Continuous processing up to 10,000 lbs/hr -> /", "Nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units installed -> /", "TurboChef: only industrial oven with microwave, convection, and steam heating -> /", "Industries served: Meat, Poultry, Alternative Protein, Pet Food, Fish, Snacks -> /", "Provides process development, plant layout, custom equipment design -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in manufacturing equipment for the protein and alternative protein products industry.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alkar-rapidpak-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='All About Electronics operates from Lyndonville, Vermont, where owner Marc Plourde has provided electronics repair and IT services across a 100-mile radius of the Littleton area for more than a decade. The business is owner‑operated and staffed by technicians holding both Microsoft A+ and Apple certifications.

The shop handles computer and laptop repair, virus removal, data recovery and backup, screen replacements for phones and tablets, soldering on motherboards and power jacks, and repair of televisions and video‑game consoles. It also builds custom desktops, sells refurbished systems starting at $99, offers remote assistance, server installation, and networking services, and provides loaner computers while a customer’s device is being serviced.

Pickup and delivery are available within 30 miles of Lyndonville.

