UPDATE companies SET description='Altek Electronics Inc., now operating as a Cyient DLM company, is headquartered in Torrington, Connecticut. The business was founded in 1972 by Stephen Altschuler, an electrical engineer with degrees from the University of Connecticut and Yale University. Altschuler previously held leadership roles at Computer Dynamics and Adage Inc. before establishing Altek to serve the electronics assembly market.

The firm provides full-service electronics manufacturing, including surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, BGA placement, selective and wave soldering, wire and cable harness fabrication, conformal coating, and box-build system integration. Operations are supported by equipment such as the ERSA Versaflow 3/66 selective soldering system, a PVA6000 conformal coating machine with IR2000 curing oven, and automated component counting and barcode traceability systems. The facility employs more than 130 people and handles programs ranging from prototype runs to full-rate production.

Altek serves original equipment manufacturers in the medical, aerospace, defense, telecommunications, industrial/commercial, and transportation sectors. The company was an early adopter of AS9100, achieving “C” level certification and later upgrading to the “D” revision in April 2017. Its quality system is also certified to ISO 9001, ISO 13485 for medical devices, and IATF 16949 for automotive, and it maintains ITAR registration for defense-related work.

Altschuler’s founding philosophy centered on customer satisfaction, on-time bill payment, and a reputation for reliability. The company states it is dedicated to offering the highest quality electronics at the most competitive price without compromising its core beliefs, a principle that has guided its growth over five decades.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949','RoHS','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (Printed Circuit Board Assembly)", "SMT Assembly", "Through Hole Assembly", "BGA Placement", "Wire & Cable Harness", "Conformal Coating", "Test", "High Voltage Soldering", "Selective Solder", "Box Build & System Integration", "Wave Soldering", "Leadless Device Placement", "Traceability", "Component Engineering", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) feedback", "Test fixture maintenance and development", "Component obsolescence mitigation"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Telecommunications", "Industrial/Commercial", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["ERSA Versaflow 3/66", "PVA6000 Conformal Coating Machine", "IR2000 Curing Oven", "MakerBot 3D Extrusion Printer", "Contact Systems CS-400 Component Locators", "Optical Control OC Scan CCX.3 Component Counter", "Barcodes Part Marking Barcode Reader System"], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ITAR registered for defense work", "130+ employees supporting prototype to production", "Integrated box build and system integration reduces hand-offs", "Early adopter of AS9100 and ISO 13485 for medical"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Torrington, Connecticut -> db", "Founded 1972 by Stephen Altschuler -> /", "Stephen Altschuler background (UConn, Yale, Computer Dynamics, Adage) -> /", "David Altschuler CEO, joined 1992 -> /about-us", "130+ employees (Travis Benningfield bio) -> /about-us", "Capabilities: PCB assembly, SMT, through-hole, BGA, wire harness, conformal coating, test, selective solder, wave solder, box build, leadless placement, traceability -> /about-us", "Equipment: ERSA Versaflow 3/66, PVA6000, IR2000, MakerBot, Contact Systems CS-400, Optical Control OC Scan CCX.3, Barcode system -> /, /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001, AS9100D (April 2017), ISO 13485, IATF 16949, RoHS, ITAR -> /, /about-us, db", "Industries: Medical, Aerospace, Defense, Telecommunications, Industrial/Commercial, Transportation -> /", "Volume: Prototype to production -> /", "Founding philosophy: customer satisfaction, on-time payment, reputation -> /", "Quality statement: highest quality at competitive price without compromising core beliefs -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Altek Electronics offers printed circuit board assembly services to OEMs who sell products used in the telecommunications industry.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "130+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='altek-electronics-inc-a-cyient-dlm-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Earthfirst Films, a division of Aluf Plastics, is headquartered in Columbus, Ohio, with additional manufacturing sites in Orangeburg, New York, and Sulphur Springs, Texas. The business traces its roots to 1949 when Joe Tatem founded Plastic Suppliers as a privately held corporation in Blackwood, New Jersey. In 2025 the Earthfirst Films brand was acquired by API, continuing its focus on sustainable packaging.

The company manufactures compostable sealant films, barrier sealant films, and laminates using blown film extrusion and cast-and-tenter extrusion technologies. Its Columbus campus operates a blown film facility and a tenter film facility supported by an on-site laboratory equipped with two lab extruders for tensile, barrier, FTIR, and microscopy testing. Capabilities include lamination, high-speed slitting, converting, and fast prototyping with small-batch production runs.

Earthfirst Films serves the food, beverage, medical, personal care, office, industrial, and broader consumer packaged goods (CPG) sectors. Its films are used in applications such as flow wrap, shrink sleeve decoration, and print web structures, targeting brands that require certified home-compostable or industrial-compostable packaging solutions.

The company states its mission is to create sustainable solutions through open collaboration. It highlights a legacy of over 20 years in biopolymer film extrusion, holding several patents on compostable sealant films, and offering materials beyond PLA, including PHA and other biobased polymers. The 2019 SQF certification for its blown film facility underscores a commitment to food-grade packaging standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','SQF (Safe Quality Food)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion", "Cast and tenter extrusion", "Lamination", "High-speed slitting", "Converting", "Laboratory testing (tensile, barrier analysis, FTIR, microscopy)", "Prototyping", "Small-batch production"], "industries": ["Food", "Beverage", "Medical", "Personal care", "Office", "Industrial", "Consumer packaged goods (CPG)"], "materials": ["PLA (Poly Lactic Acid)", "PHA (Polyhydroxyalkanoates)", "Biobased polymers", "Polystyrene (Polyflex)"], "equipment": ["Blown film lines", "Cast and tenter extrusion lines", "Lab extruders", "High-speed slitters"], "volume": "Prototype and small-batch production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented blown extrusion process for biopolymer films", "Small-batch production and fast prototyping of laminates", "SQF-certified blown film facility for food-contact packaging", "Over 20 years of biopolymer film extrusion experience", "Multiple patents on compostable sealant films"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Columbus, Ohio; additional sites Orangeburg NY, Sulphur Springs TX -> /about-us", "Founded 1949 by Joe Tatem as Plastic Suppliers in Blackwood NJ -> /about-us", "2025 API Acquisition of Earthfirst Films -> /about-us", "Manufactures compostable sealant, barrier sealant films, laminates -> /, /about-us", "Processes: blown film extrusion, cast and tenter extrusion, lamination, slitting, converting -> /services", "Facilities: blown film facility 2450 Marilyn Lane, tenter film facility 2400 Marilyn Lane -> /