UPDATE companies SET description='American Alloy Fabrication, Inc. (AAFI) began in 1980 as a one‑man welding shop in Huntsville, Alabama, founded to serve local industries with precision welding services.

By 1987 the company had incorporated and moved into a new facility that has since been expanded multiple times. Today AAFI operates as a vertically integrated contract manufacturer offering sheet metal fabrication (laser cutting, CNC turret punching, CNC forming), CNC and manual machining, welding (MIG, TIG, spot, robotic), metal finishing, deburring, polishing, mechanical assembly, and packaging, crating and logistics support. The shop also provides design‑for‑manufacturability assistance, prototype development, production manufacturing and complete project management.

The company’s customer base spans diverse industries; its first major contract came from a local engine manufacturer that needed a reusable shipping rack, a project that launched AAFI into large‑scale contract manufacturing. Since then the firm has supplied fabricated parts, industrial enclosures, custom weldments and mechanical assemblies to a range of industrial clients.

AAFI emphasizes continuous investment in advanced manufacturing technology and a quality system that consistently achieves above 95 % acceptance and on‑time delivery. Inspection capabilities include coordinate measuring machines, optical comparators and laser scanners. The company’s stated goal is to build long‑term partnerships by acting as an extension of its customers’ organizations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet Metal Fabrication", "Laser Cutting", "CNC Turret Punching", "CNC Forming", "CNC & Manual Machining", "Welding (MIG, TIG, Spot, Robotic)", "Metal Finishing", "Deburring", "Polishing", "Mechanical Assembly", "Packaging, Crating and Logistics Support", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Prototype Development", "Production Manufacturing", "Complete Project Management"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Coordinate measuring machines", "Optical comparators", "Laser scanners"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Continuous investment in latest manufacturing technologies", "Quality acceptance and delivery performance consistently above 95%", "In\u2011house inspection with CMMs, optical comparators and laser scanners", "Vertically integrated from design support through final assembly", "Lean manufacturing and continuous improvement focus"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 as one-man shop in Huntsville, Alabama -> /about-us", "Incorporated and moved to current facility in 1987 -> /about-us", "First major contract with local engine manufacturer for reusable shipping rack -> /about-us", "Vertically integrated contract manufacturer offering fabricated parts, enclosures, weldments, assemblies -> /about-us", "Capabilities: sheet metal fabrication, laser cutting, CNC turret punching, CNC forming, CNC & manual machining, welding (MIG, TIG, spot, robotic), metal finishing, deburring, polishing, mechanical assembly, packaging/crating/logistics, DFM, prototype development, production manufacturing, complete project management -> /", "Quality acceptance and delivery performance above 95% -> /quality", "Inspection equipment: CMMs, optical comparators, laser scanners -> /quality", "Focus on continuous improvement, lean manufacturing -> / (home page description)", "Goal to develop long-term relationships, become extension of customer organization -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Huntsville, Alabama -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today AAFI is a full service, vertically integrated contract manufacturer supplying customers with fabricated parts, industrial enclosures, custom weldments and mechanical assemblies.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-alloy-fabrication-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Auto Parts operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility on five acres at 1807 North 16th Street in Omaha, Nebraska. The company has served the greater Omaha area for more than 50 years, though a precise founding year is not publicly stated. Ownership details and founder names are not disclosed; long-time staff members Dan (with the company since 2001, 35 years industry experience) and Mark (since 2000, 19 years experience) are highlighted as parts specialists.

The business supplies domestic and foreign used, remanufactured, aftermarket, and new OEM surplus auto parts. Inventory spans engines, transmissions, doors, radiators, differentials, transfer cases, tires, and wheels. The company offers a parts locator service, coast-to-coast shipping within the continental United States (airbags excluded), local delivery, and 24/7 online purchasing through an eBay storefront.

Customers include fellow automotive recyclers, independent garages, collision repair shops, and individual vehicle owners. The company positions itself as a resource for both trade buyers and retail consumers seeking foreign and domestic light-truck and passenger-car components.

