UPDATE companies SET description='American Steel Fabrication was founded in 1994 by Tim Thomas and a group of his customers in Pevely, Missouri, a suburb of St. Louis. The company remains locally owned and operated, with Thomas serving as president and drawing on experience that began in the steel construction industry at age 15.

The firm runs a complete fabrication facility supplying both structural and reinforcing steel. It stocks carbon, stainless, and aluminum products in forms including beams, angles, channels, pipe, tube, plate, bar, and sheet, while also fabricating embeds, pipe bollards, adjustable columns, H-pile, joist and deck, and epoxy-coated rebar. Services extend to same-day pickup, next-day delivery, and on-site ironworker erection and installation.

Customers span commercial, industrial, and infrastructure construction across the Midwest. A notable project includes the Ameren Bagnell Dam stabilization, where the company contributed to a 2,453-foot gravity dam requiring 67 post-tension anchors and 17,000 cubic yards of concrete.

