UPDATE companies SET description='Applied Molding Technologies, LLC was founded in 2006 in Frederic, Wisconsin.

The shop provides thermoplastic injection molding on all-electric presses ranging from 55 to 850 tons of clamp force, and thermoset compression, transfer, and injection molding on presses from 150 to 300 tons. It also offers value-added mechanical assembly including heat-staking, ultrasonic inserts, sub-assemblies, kitting, and ship-direct packaging. Production runs 24/7/365 on a four-shift rotation designed to minimize start-up and shut-down scrap. Tooling is sourced both domestically and off-shore, with in-house maintenance and repair.

Applied Molding serves a global customer base with varying technical, regulatory, and commercial requirements. Its thermoset capabilities target electrical and dielectric components as well as large or thick-section parts, while its thermoplastic work spans commodity and engineering-grade resins. The company scales engineering, quality, and program-management support to each customer''s needs.

The business was built on the premise that domestic manufacturing could compete through a fundamentally different operating model rather than low-wage competition. Its founders designed the company for efficiency, customization, and adaptability—retaining core capabilities in-house while partnering for ancillary functions, and continuously revisiting processes through structured improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding", "Thermoset compression molding", "Thermoset transfer molding", "Thermoset injection molding", "Mechanical assembly (heat-staking, ultrasonic inserts, sub-assemblies, kitting, packaging, ship-direct)", "Tooling services (new mold builds, off-shore programs, tool maintenance & repair)", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) analysis", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Process-controlled production with full traceability"], "industries": ["Electrical components"], "materials": ["Commodity resins", "Engineering grade resins", "Thermoset materials"], "equipment": ["All-electric injection presses (55-850T)", "Thermoset presses (150-300T)"], "volume": "Low to high volume production; 24/7/365 continuous operation", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 continuous production since inception with four-shift rotation", "Dual material expertise: thermoplastic and thermoset under one roof", "Domestic and off-shore tooling management with vetted sources", "Customized program support scaled to each customer''s requirements", "Process-controlled, ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Frederic, Wisconsin -> db, /", "Thermoplastic injection molding 55-850T -> /, /capabilities", "Thermoset compression, transfer, injection molding 150-300T -> /, /capabilities", "Mechanical assembly services -> /, /capabilities", "24/7/365 production with four-shift rotation -> /, /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /capabilities", "Domestic and off-shore tooling -> /, /about", "Serves customers globally -> db, /", "Electrical/dielectric components and large/thick-section parts -> /capabilities", "Commodity and engineering grade resins -> /capabilities", "Heat-staking, ultrasonic inserts, sub-assemblies, kitting, ship-direct -> /capabilities", "DFM analysis -> /capabilities", "Process-controlled production, full traceability -> /capabilities", "Company designed for efficiency, customization, adaptability -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "delivers thermoplastic injection and thermoset compression, transfer and injection molding", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='applied-molding-technologies-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Applied Plastics was founded in 1976 in Portland, Oregon, where it operates a 30,000-square-foot manufacturing facility. The company has remained at this location for nearly five decades, serving customers across the United States, Canada, and internationally.

The shop specializes in machining and fabricating plastic parts, offering services that include acrylic fabrication, laser cutting and engraving, and precision cutting of full sheets to size. It also extrudes its own UHMW board stock and reprocesses recycled UHMW into usable material. The facility handles sheets, rods, and tubes in a variety of plastics, though headcount and annual volume are not disclosed.

Applied Plastics serves a range of markets, producing components for retail displays, industrial plastic applications, and extruded UHMW board stock.

The company emphasizes a personal service guarantee, with machinists and fabricators working directly with clients on material selection and design. It also highlights environmental practices, including a near zero-waste operation that recycles acrylic scrap, extrudes recycled UHMW, and uses evaporative cooling and motion-activated lighting to reduce energy consumption.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic machining", "Acrylic fabrication", "Laser cutting", "Laser engraving", "Sheet cutting to size", "UHMW extrusion", "Recycled material extrusion"], "industries": ["Retail displays", "Industrial plastics", "Extruded UHMW board stock"], "materials": ["Acrylic", "UHMW", "Recycled UHMW", "Plastic sheets", "Plastic rods", "Plastic tubes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Personal service guarantee with direct machinist-to-customer collaboration", "Near zero-waste facility recycling acrylic scrap and extruding recycled UHMW", "Energy-efficient shop using evaporative cooling and motion-activated lighting", "In-house extrusion of UHMW board stock and recycled materials"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 -> db", "30,000 sf facility in Portland, Oregon -> /", "Plastic machining and acrylic fabrication services -> /", "Laser cutting and engraving -> /", "Full sheets cut to size -> /", "Serves customers in United States, Canada, and beyond -> /", "Markets: retail displays, industrial plastics, extruded UHMW board stock -> /", "Personal service guarantee -> /", "Near zero-waste operation, acrylic scrap recycling, recycled UHMW extrusion -> /about-us", "Evaporative cooling and motion-activated lighting for energy reduction -> /about-us", "Works with sheets, rods, tubes in various plastics -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All of our products are proudly manufactured at our 30,000 sf facility located in Portland Oregon.", "founded_year": "1976", "e